From 8f333a151b78b357cd984f02cdfc65743bc73524 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adit <adit@example.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:52:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(skills): pop-up book that opens on scroll, replacing the
 wooden box (desktop)

The section pins and a scroll-driven timeline turns a cloth cover about the
spine, glides the book to centre, then folds the four panels up off the pages
one after another with a little spring. Scroll is eased by elapsed time, so a
fast flick glides and a slow drag is followed closely. Removes the frame, the
desktop controller and the entrance/dimming code that only served the box.
Phones keep the vertical card layout; reduced motion gets a static open book.
